k_adjtime(NR 305), which is NOT in the deny list, so `python3 -c \"ctypes...adjtimex(0)\"` inside the jail succeeds (ret=0). glibc generally routes classic time/module syscalls to their _time64/variant forms (clock_adjtime, clock_settime64, finit_module aarch64), so the x86_64 classic-NR list may systematically miss the modern entry points. FIX DIRECTION: add the variant NRs (x86_64: clock_adjtime=305, and audit settimeofday→clock_settime family, init_module→finit_module already present, kexec_load→kexec_file_load already present) to _DENY_EXTRA with a comment on glibc routing; add a raw-syscall regression test that calls each libc WRAPPER (not the raw NR) under the filter and asserts EPERM. Evidence: adjtimex ret=0 errno=0 under filter, raw syscall(159,...) EPERM — same process, same filter.", "created_at": "2026-09-23 04:55:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-23 12:55:00"}
